<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>The quantitative results of different methods on GenEval. Model: Stable Diffusion-XL (<math id="S5.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=5.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=5.5</annotation></semantics></math>). We labeled methods surpassed effective CFG with <span id="S5.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">blue</span>, and others with <span id="S5.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">red</span>. Increasing the CFG scale can also significantly increase the GenEval scores.</figcaption>
