<a href="#S1.p2.1" title="1 Introduction ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§1</span></a>.
</span></li>
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>LLM Usage</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, no Large Language Model (LLM) was employed as a research or writing tool. All research conception, data analysis, writing, and editing were independently accomplished by the author.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Experimental Settings</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All our experiments were conducted on NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4090 GPUs with 24GB VRAM.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In SD-XL, we use guidance scale <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=5.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=5.5</annotation></semantics></math> and inference step <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=50</annotation></semantics></math>. For Z-Sampling, we use inversion guidance scale <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\mathrm{inv}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>inv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\mathrm{inv}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, optimization steps <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=T</annotation></semantics></math>. For PAG, we use PAG scale <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=3</annotation></semantics></math>, and apply PAG on layer “mid” of the backbone of SD-XL. For CFG++, we use guidance scale <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=0.4</annotation></semantics></math>. For TDG, we use <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=1.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=1.8</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=2.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=2.6</annotation></semantics></math>. For APG, we use guidance scale <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=15</annotation></semantics></math>. For FreeU, we use <math id="A2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}=1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}=1.3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{2}=1.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{2}=1.4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>. For SAG, we use SAG scale <math id="A2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>. For SEG, we use SEG scale <math id="A2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\mathrm{seg}}=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>seg</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\mathrm{seg}}=3</annotation></semantics></math>, standard deviation of Gauusian blur <math id="A2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma=100</annotation></semantics></math>, and apply on layer “mid” of the backbone of SD-XL.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In SD-2.1, we use guidance scale <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=5.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=5.5</annotation></semantics></math> and inference step <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=50</annotation></semantics></math>. For Z-Sampling, we use inversion guidance scale <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\mathrm{inv}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>inv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\mathrm{inv}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, optimization steps <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=T</annotation></semantics></math>. For PAG, we use PAG scale <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=3</annotation></semantics></math>, and apply PAG on layer “mid” of the backbone of SD-XL. For CFG++, we use guidance scale <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=0.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=0.4</annotation></semantics></math>. For FreeU, we use <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{1}=1.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{1}=1.4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{2}=1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{2}=1.6</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{2}=0.2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{2}=0.2</annotation></semantics></math>. For SAG, we use SAG scale <math id="A2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=0.75" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.75</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=0.75</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In SD-3.5, we use 4-bit NormalFloat quantization to run on RTX-4090, with guidance scale <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=4.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=4.5</annotation></semantics></math> and inference step <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=32</annotation></semantics></math>. For Z-Sampling, we use inversion guidance scale <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\mathrm{inv}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>inv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\mathrm{inv}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, optimization steps <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=T</annotation></semantics></math>. For PAG, we use PAG scale <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s=3</annotation></semantics></math>, and apply PAG on layer “13” of the backbone of SD-3.5. For TDG, we use <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g=1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g=1.6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=2.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=2.4</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">In DiT-XL/2, we use guidance scale <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=4</annotation></semantics></math> and timestep <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=50</annotation></semantics></math>. For Z-Sampling, we use inversion guidance scale <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{\mathrm{inv}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>inv</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{\mathrm{inv}}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, optimization steps <math id="A2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=T</annotation></semantics></math>. For CFG++, we use guidance scale <math id="A2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Transcedent Diffusion Guidance</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we will present limitations of previous guidance techniques. After that, we will introduce the proposed method transcendent diffusion guidance (TDG), and illustrate how can we improve the sampling process of diffusion models by enlarging search space.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Motivation</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Previous improvements to CFG have been limited to the guidance scale <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> or use self-defined functions to substitute <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, these methods are limited to the operation in Eq <a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2 Diffusion Guidance and Sampling ‣ 2 Related Work ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>: interpolation between the two outputs of the diffusion model.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To solve this problem, we need to expand the search space of the sampling process. Obviously, due to the search space of CFG restricted on a line, we only need to have a point outside of this line to obtain the whole hyperplane as the search space. Besides, the point should be acquired through the text prompt <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math> without introducing any additional inputs.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Driven by the analysis above, we propose transcendent diffusion guidance to improve the sampling process of diffusion models, which illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3 Guidance Matters to Evaluation ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Specifically, TDG corrupts the text prompt <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math> to create a weakened text prompt <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then use the noise prediction network <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> to acquire the weak conditional score <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{weak}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>weak</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{weak}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining with <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{cond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>cond</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{cond}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{uncond}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{uncond}}</annotation></semantics></math> in CFG, we can expand the search space to the entire hyperplane. During the sampling process, larger search space will accelerate the convergence of latent towards the optimal solution, thereby improving the generation quality of the model.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Weak Condition</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subsection, we will provide a detailed explanation on how to obtain a weak condition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As mentioned in the main text, many works demonstrated that introduce an additional weak model or weak condition could improve the generation performance.
Meanwhile, they should avoid introducing any additional input and be computationally efficient. Therefore, we obtain the weak condition outside of CFG by modifying the text prompt.
Specifically, consider a text prompt <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}=[c_{1},c_{2},\dots,c_{n}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}=[c_{1},c_{2},\dots,c_{n}]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th token of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math>. We randomly choose some tokens with index <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, and replace them with empty token <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{*}_{i}=\begin{cases}\varnothing,&amp;i\in\mathcal{I}\\
c_{i},&amp;i\notin\mathcal{I}\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{*}_{i}=\begin{cases}\varnothing,&amp;i\in\mathcal{I}\\
c_{i},&amp;i\notin\mathcal{I}\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">By combining these new tokens together, we obtained the weakened prompt <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}^{*}=[c_{1}^{*},\dots,c_{n}^{*}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}^{*}=[c_{1}^{*},\dots,c_{n}^{*}]</annotation></semantics></math>.
In practice, <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{I}|=\frac{n}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{I}|=\frac{n}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which means we randomly replace half tokens in <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math>.
On the one hand, the modified prompt only requires the original prompt to be obtained without introducing additional input.
On the other hand, to obtain <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, it only needs to be calculated at the beginning, which is computationally efficient compared to those methods need to manipulating attention maps at every denoising step.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the weak conditional score is given by:</p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t}=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{c}^{*})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>weak</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t}=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{c}^{*}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Algorithm</h3>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> The Sampling of Transcendent Diffusion Guidance</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> text condition <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}</annotation></semantics></math>, guidance scale factor <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, balance scale factor <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>, random replace ratio <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{c}^{*}=\mathrm{random\_replace}(\mathbf{c},\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>random</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>replace</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{c}^{*}=\mathrm{random\_replace}(\mathbf{c},\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐈</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{T}\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\mathbf{I})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T,T-1,\dots,1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T,T-1,\dots,1</annotation></semantics></math>  <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{uncond}}^{t}=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>uncond</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{uncond}}^{t}=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{cond}}^{t}=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>cond</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐜</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{cond}}^{t}=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{c})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\mathrm{weak}}^{t}=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{c}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>weak</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐜</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\mathrm{weak}}^{t}=\epsilon_{\theta}(\mathbf{x}_{t},\mathbf{c}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\epsilon}_{t}=\frac{1}{2}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}+\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t})+\frac{\omega\cdot g\cdot\beta}{\beta+1}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t})+\frac{\omega\cdot g}{\beta+1}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t})\cdot\frac{\left\|\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}\right\|}{\left\|\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t}\right\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>weak</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>weak</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>weak</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\epsilon}_{t}=\frac{1}{2}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}+\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t})+\frac{\omega\cdot g\cdot\beta}{\beta+1}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t})+\frac{\omega\cdot g}{\beta+1}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t})\cdot\frac{\left\|\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}\right\|}{\left\|\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t}\right\|}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
              <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{t-1}\sim\mathcal{N}(\frac{1}{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}(\mathrm{x}_{t}-\frac{\beta_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\tilde{\epsilon}_{t}),\Sigma_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{t-1}\sim\mathcal{N}(\frac{1}{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}(\mathrm{x}_{t}-\frac{\beta_{t}}{\sqrt{1-\bar{\alpha}_{t}}}\tilde{\epsilon}_{t}),\Sigma_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              
              
             <span id="alg1.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{x}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{x}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">After obtaining the weak condition, we can construct the hyperplane through an extra guidance term. Compared to CFG in Eq <a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2 Diffusion Guidance and Sampling ‣ 2 Related Work ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, TDG reformulated the diffusion score in each denoising step with following add-on:</p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\epsilon}_{t}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\epsilon}_{t}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}+\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t})+\frac{\omega\cdot g\cdot\beta}{\beta+1}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t})+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>weak</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}+\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t})+\frac{\omega\cdot g\cdot\beta}{\beta+1}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t})+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E15Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E15Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\omega\cdot g}{\beta+1}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t})\cdot\frac{\left\|\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}\right\|}{\left\|\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t}\right\|}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>weak</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>weak</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\omega\cdot g}{\beta+1}(\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t})\cdot\frac{\left\|\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}\right\|}{\left\|\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}-\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t}\right\|},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> are guidance scale factor and balance scale factor, respectively.
For noise prediction network <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{\theta}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{\theta}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, the linear combination of conditional score <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the weak conditional score <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>weak</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\mathrm{weak}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the unconditional score <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> will create three non-collinear points, thus creating a hyperplane. While the original CFG only limits its search space the combination of <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>cond</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\mathrm{cond}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>uncond</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\mathrm{uncond}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is a straight line.
Therefore, the model can have a hyperplane as the search space, which transcend the restrictions of the original search space of CFG.
We give a brief illustration in Fig <a href="#A3.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ C.3 Algorithm ‣ Appendix C Transcedent Diffusion Guidance ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. And the hyperparameter grid search result was illustrated in Fig <a href="#A3.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ C.3 Algorithm ‣ Appendix C Transcedent Diffusion Guidance ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The pseudo-code is provided in Alg <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ C.3 Algorithm ‣ Appendix C Transcedent Diffusion Guidance ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Fig <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3 Guidance Matters to Evaluation ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> also briefly illustrates the differences between TDG and CFG.
Qualitative comparison results are presented in Fig <a href="#A3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ C.3 Algorithm ‣ Appendix C Transcedent Diffusion Guidance ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
The hyperparameters of TDG are determined through grid search, and the criteria is HPSv2 winning rate compared to original CFG. The results can be found in Fig <a href="#A3.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ C.3 Algorithm ‣ Appendix C Transcedent Diffusion Guidance ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.
Meanwhile, we give an analysis on the number of inference step <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> to demonstrate the superiority of TDG. In Fig <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.3 Algorithm ‣ Appendix C Transcedent Diffusion Guidance ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, TDG with <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\!=\!16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!=\!16</annotation></semantics></math> achieved comparable performance on CFG with <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\!=\!20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!=\!20</annotation></semantics></math>, and TDG always maintain better performance than CFG when <math id="A3.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\!\geq\!16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\!\geq\!16</annotation></semantics></math>. We also present ablation results of TDG in Fig <a href="#A3.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ C.3 Algorithm ‣ Appendix C Transcedent Diffusion Guidance ‣ Guidance Matters: Rethinking the Evaluation Pitfall for Text-to-Image Generation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>. There is no significant performance degradation when mask ratio smaller than 0.6.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F6" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.22570v1/qualitative_result.png" id="A3.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:550/228;" width="550" height="228" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span>The qualitative results of TDG. </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A3.F7.2" class="ltx_p ltx_align_center ltx_align_center"><span id="A3.F7.2.1" class="ltx_text"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.22570v1/timestep_curve.svg" id="A3.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:314/236;" width="314" height="236"></object></span></p>
